# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 130's class, lane recovery-b3 (the recovery
# instrument's pairs: `single-quotes` and `string-open` as the first mistake
# hid a signature's own). Symptom: an `extern` whose header the lexer refused,
# a string never closed or one in single quotes, or none at all before the
# line's end, recovered to the next declaration, and every signature below
# went unread, its own mistakes unsaid. Cause: `group_header` handed the
# whole group to the recovery whenever no string stood where the header
# goes. Now the header's mistake is the head's one message, and the
# signatures below are read as a group's (`parse/group.group_header`).

extern "never_closed.h  #~ unterminated_string
    function f(x: i64): i64  #~ expected_end_of_line

extern 'single_quoted.h'  #~ char_literal
    function g(x: i64): i64  #~ expected_end_of_line

extern  #~ expected_extern_header
    function h(x: i64): i64  #~ expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)
